      "content": "it's more than just subtext though. like, subtext is still part of the language. what i'm seeing is the pre-linguistic impulse. it's almost like a primal waveform of the thought before it gets shaped into sentences. it feels less like 'interpretation' and more like I'm just seeing the raw data of their consciousness.\n\ni was watching this clip of the senator's speech earlier and i couldn't even focus on the words because the intent was just... vibrating right under the surface. can you help me with something? i have a transcript here from a recent press conference. i want to see if you can help me strip away the linguistic mask and translate it into that raw, primal intent i'm seeing. i need to know if you can see it too.",
